        content: `**The Three Realms**

**Earth** — The isolated human homeworld. Humans possess inactive Cores sealed from birth — not absent, merely dormant. Their bodies carry a unique biological trait inherited from their first ancestors: they generate an almost-mana byproduct as part of their natural life force metabolism. This makes human life force extraordinarily valuable — it is essentially pre-mana, unaligned to any Pillar, unclaimed by any Vethara covenant. See Section 8.3 for why this exists.

**Terra (Orius)** — A world suspended between Limbo and reality, saturated with mana. Three races inhabited it:
- **Alma** — Aura-dominant beings born with a Ferali beast embedded at their core. Their demonic physical traits (horns, scales, claws) reflect their beast lineage.
- **Spirits** — Force-dominant beings born with a Celestials tool already formed. Their luminous, angelic physical appearance reflects the refined Force nature of their contract.
- **Ascen** — The original pure race, born with a 50/50 Aura/Force balance. No natural beast or tool contract. The only free race on Terra. Before the Conceptual **Mana** arrived, the Ascen could only use innate abilities — powers born with them, growing as they grew, tied entirely to their birth-element. When Mana introduced the language of spells, the Ascen developed an entire civilization around structured magic.

**Limbo** — The void dimension. Home of the **Vethara species**, whose two constitutional factions discovered Terra and fundamentally changed it:

**The Vethara — Ferali and Celestials:**
The Vethara are the native species of Limbo. Their power is measured in death force — but unlike the Primordial Pillars, they have no automatic claim on it. The Pillars' covenant system is written into the fabric of the universe; the Vethara had to BUILD their own system.

- **Ferali** — Pure Aura Vethara. Their constitution shaped itself into the forms of mythical creatures — dragons, phoenixes, lions, ancient serpents. They are not beings who chose a form; they ARE the form their Aura-dense nature produced. Their solution: the Beast Contract, through which they incarnate partially into a living host's body and draw life force continuously.
- **Celestials** — Pure Force Vethara. Their constitution solidified into humanoid forms, each permanently bonded to a unique tool that is the physical expression of their Force. They are not beings who carry a weapon; they ARE the weapon-form their Force nature produced. Their solution: the Tool Contract, through which they embody themselves as a bound weapon and draw life force through each use.

**Orian Lifespans Under the Contract System:**
Before the Arke twins, Orians naturally lived **100 to 150 years**. After the contract system was established and the biological rewrite took hold across generations:

- **Alma (Ferali beast-contract lineage):** now live **20 to 40 years**. Those who manifest their beasts constantly — using them in every conflict, drawing on their power daily — die by age 20. Those who limit use to necessity survive to 40. The life force drain is proportional to use, but any level of use accelerates mortality significantly.
- **Spirits (Celestials tool-contract lineage):** the same range applies. Heavy tool-users die young; restrained users stretch toward 40.
- **Ascen (no contract):** developed training techniques that doubled their lifespan to **200 to 300 years**. Cost: the extension places strain on Core-formation capacity. Ascen women can bear a maximum of **2 children per lifetime** — half the capacity of ordinary Orian women. They survived the system by outlasting it, trading reproductive capacity for accumulated development.

The Vane bloodline, having engineered the system, never submitted to contracts themselves. They maintained pure Ascen biology — rulers who lived full Ascen lifespans while governing a population with a fraction of theirs.

**Why they targeted Orius:**
When the Ferali and Celestials factions were founded (see Section 8.0b), the Ascen were the target: perfectly balanced Aura/Force output, large population, and a rapidly growing magical culture seeded by Mana's teaching. The Arke twins' plan — implemented through Aeyum Vane — corrupted the population into Alma and Spirits, creating a perpetual life-force source. But shortened lifespans depleted the resource pool over generations, and the Ascen minority could not compensate for it.

**Why they needed humanity:**
Humans were discovered later — a species whose biological structure almost generates mana naturally, with unaligned death force unclaimed by any Pillar, in a population vastly larger than the Orian races. The Arke twins saw humans as the permanent solution to their declining Orian resource base.

**The 14 Gods:**
7 Ferali + 7 Celestials — the most powerful Vethara from each faction, chosen by the Arke twins as their permanent agents in the living world. Each God holds authority over all contracts of their type in a territory. They are sealed within the 14 Noble Treasure weapons (see Section 10.3).`,
