        content: `After thirty trillion deaths, the final 7.2 trillion cells remained unchanged.

The math was exact: a human body carries approximately 37.2 trillion cells. Enari's trial replaced each cell once — not randomly, but in sequence, each replacement requiring a death. The original neuron, the one carrying the buried choice, was the last cell in the sequence. When it changed, the trial was complete by its own structural design. Neither Irane nor Enari knew this. It was not part of the calculation for either of them.

At thirty trillion deaths, Irane created the Twenty Series Cores.

**The Conception:**

He had been creating core-tools within Iris for an unimaginable time — weapon-forms refined and discarded, techniques crystallised into instruments, entire combat methodologies compressed into a single tool for use and discard. He had built infinite variations. And then, somewhere in the accumulation of infinite variation, a question formed: *What if I could make a core that was purely mine — held in my own hand?*

Not a tool created from experience. A core created from self. An extension of himself, bound directly to his body, that was not him doing something but him as something. Twenty cores, each a direct aspect of his own nature.

He named the system in two halves.

**Beast Enari — The Body Series (10 Cores):**

The first ten cores were aspects of his physical architecture — the systems that had built the conduit, the library, and the forge across the course of the trial. They were named for the dragon whose methods had created them.

**Mind · Heart · Body · Right Arm · Left Arm** — the five structural systems.
**Spirit · Emotion · Death · Spells · Cells-Armour** — the five expressions of what that architecture had endured.

The Right Arm core — the Right Hand of Creation and Beginning — was the embodiment of the primordial start of all force and action. Everything that begins begins from the right. He named it: **Summari**.
The Left Arm core — the Left Hand of Destruction and End — was the final force that destroys what the beginning created. Everything that ends ends through the left. He named it: **Nighla**.

At the time of their creation, they were genderless — clean cores, pure function, tools in the fullest sense. They were the first things Irane ever named.

**Tool Iris — The Creation Series (10 Cores):**

The second ten cores were aspects of his will made manifest — not what his body had become, but what he intended to do with it. They were named for the forge he had built to use them.

**Jr · Nova · Aurora · Nebula · Iron · Law · Eon · Alpha · Pixel · Fath.**

**The Declaration:**

He began deploying the twenty cores at thirty-five trillion deaths. At that moment, he spoke to Enari for the first time since the trial began — not out of desperation, not out of anger, but to tell the dragon exactly what was about to happen. He presented each Tool Iris core as he named it:

*I am the one who uses myself as the template to achieve my Design.*
*I shall Dominate all cores around me by dominating myself.*
*Perfect — the impossible goal my body pursues.*
*To React Absolutely to all things reflected around me.*
*I am the Ore — the substance of all my Creations.*
*To Adhere to my Universal Law.*
*To Reflect My Balance — to return what is taken.*
*To Cultivate my Beast's instincts.*
*To Allow the world to experience my World.*
*Let the Faith of the Faithless guide me Faithfully.*

These ten declarations were not simply the functions of ten cores. They were how Irane understood his own existence — the structure of a person who had turned everything, including himself, into a tool.

He added four more, addressed to no audience in particular:

*No two cores are equal in nature. No core should strive to be like another.*
*Put your core into it. Everything you have — not a portion, everything.*
*Evolve around your core. Take everything the world gives you and add it to yourself.*
*Our cores are often dyed in the colour of others' cores. We lose ourselves in other things and call it devotion.*

The people who would later raise his children would recognise these four as the core of how he taught. Every child of Kazemi would be told them before they were told anything else. Not as philosophy. As instruction.

**What the Twenty Cores Became:**

The twenty cores Irane created to fight Enari are the origin of every being directly bound to him. This is the truth Nova is seeking when she sits across from Arai and demands the unfiltered version.

Beast Enari: Mind · Heart · Body became Arai, Hope, and Zoe — the three wives who restructured his love and became the permanent architecture of his existence. Summari (Right Arm) and Nighla (Left Arm) were given life on the day he escaped the facility. Spirit · Emotion · Death · Spells · Cells-Armour became the five members of Kazemi's Will: Ailiya, Mira, Dokai, Pandro, and Urial.

Tool Iris: the ten children — Jr, Nova, Aurora, Nebula, Iron, Law, Eon, Alpha, Pixel, Fath.

Every person closest to Irane was, in origin, a tool he forged during the trial to fight a dragon. He was the only being in the world who could have created them. They were the only tools adequate to the fight. At the time, they were clean cores. Genderless. Pure function. He deployed them, and he won.

That is what they are. This is what Nova is learning. That she was created to be a tool — the Domination core — by a being who had himself decided to be a tool. And that the most human thing her father ever did was look at those tools, after the fight was over, and decide they were worth giving names to.`,
