        tags: ['irane', 'facility-arc-part-3', 'core-mechanics', 'vraka', 'selis', 'gaia', 'cronus'],
        content: `Under Minia's standing order to act as the legend of Kazemi Primal prophecy — filled in, without her knowledge, from a private manuscript written by Sofia Prescian — 8 began operating from a single organizing value: a core shines brightest when it is used for a person's true will, not a lie. This produced the **choose-to-serve contract**, invented for Criya Sin and extended afterward to Mira Ardent, Pandro Lexan, and hundreds of the captured children: offer your core, and for as long as you choose to serve, his power is yours to wield. Failure carries a real cost — the core becomes his outright.

This is a fourth distinct gift-system, worth setting beside the three that already govern power transfer in the world:

— **Vraka and Selis** pre-select a comparable core for the recipient, engineered to be desirable and usable from the start — a system of assignment.
— **Gaia** enters a beast most suited to the recipient from scratch, drawing on their blood. **Cronus** uses foresight to forge the optimal tool for who the recipient will become. Both are systems of design, built around the person's biology or future.
— **Irane's** tools and beasts are built from the *core itself* — not the element, not the biology, not the future — and work only when the wielder puts their actual, true self into using it. Nothing else in the world's power systems is this difficult to master, or this impossible to use dishonestly.

This is also why he registers Namo Consa's core as "not worth absorbing," why he is drawn to moments of total honesty (Pandro and Sofia's confession scene chief among them), and why his interest in a subject's authenticity — not their raw strength — becomes the organizing principle of the entire training-era squad.`,
