        tags: ['irane', 'facility-arc-part-4', 'core-mechanics', 'core-forge', 'summari', 'nighla', 'arai', 'hope', 'zoe'],
        content: `Deep into the trial, after he began threatening Enari seriously enough to draw the first Ascendant-class spell (Time, Space, Life/Death) out of him, Irane needed a way to hold Arai, Hope, and Zoe's mana inside his own body without simply absorbing them the way he absorbed everything else. His reproductive system — altered during the trial into something with no remaining reproductive purpose in the ordinary sense — became the mechanism: a Core Forge, capable of generating new cores rather than new cells. Its first products were three replica cores, one each of Arai's, Hope's, and Zoe's present mana, built to store what he could not simply take. Its next products were the fifteen cores that make up the Will set and the ten Conceptual cores (Design through Faith) — the accumulated shape of everything he understood himself to be across trillions of deaths, tied to no single person the way the first three were.

This is the full mechanism behind a fact already on record elsewhere: **the ten Conceptual cores are the only pool from which his children can be born.** Their genetics are random — even Irane does not know in advance what a given core will become when implanted. Ember's Design core and Summari and Nighla's Beginning-Creation and Destruction-Ending cores all trace back to this same forge, not to three separate systems.

**Why Summari and Nighla Should Not Exist**

Summari and Nighla's cores are not ordinary Conceptual cores. They were built as aspects of Irane's own Mind-Heart-Body system — Beginning-Creation paired to represent the start of Kazemi's nature, Destruction-Ending to represent its end — and that pairing means their existence required the combined mana of Arai, Hope, and Zoe to be present simultaneously at conception. That condition had never occurred and, by Arai's own understanding of the architecture, should never have been able to occur through a fourth party's body. It happened anyway only because Ember, years earlier and without knowing it, had fused all three women's core-signatures into the disguise-spell Minia used to hide her own core and issue every order she gave Irane. For as long as that spell runs, Minia's body carries a live, combined proxy of Arai, Hope, and Zoe at once — which is the only reason two cores requiring all three of them could ever take root in a fourth woman entirely. It is a stated impossibility resolved by an accident nobody involved intended.

**The Command Cores and the Chains of Ventriloquist**

The cores Summari and Nighla carry are not finished versions of Arai's, Hope's, and Zoe's natures — they are early, incomplete replicas: the Electric core copied from Arai, the Energy core copied from Hope, the Nature core copied from Zoe, each missing the Time, Space, and Life/Death dimensions the real women carry. This is why the pregnancy was killing them from the start even as it kept them alive — the cores draw everything they can to try to complete themselves. Irane built a tool specifically to manage this: **the Chains of Ventriloquist**, designed to bind directly to command cores — Kazemi cores like these — and route their mana continuously between the growing cores in Minia and the real cores in Arai, Hope, and Zoe, keeping the twins developing without simply killing their hosts outright. Minia did not invent the chains and did not know what they were built for. She inherited a tool Irane made to serve his own order and turned it against him, using its Form 4 to force him toward full Conceptual precisely because it was already wired into the same architecture.

It took Irane roughly a week, once Summari and Nighla's cores stopped being hidden the way Minia's own disguised core was, to filter their signal clear of the noise the spell generated — and once it cleared, Arai felt it as a mounting headache, and Ember felt it as the design of thirty-seven trillion deaths pouring directly into a mind never built to hold any of it.`,
